From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 15:46:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 20/26] node-executor: capture first-miss wedge diagnostics

Move the maintained self-hosted runtime to Node.js 24.18.1 and require
Node major 24 for local Node actions. Align dashboard lint guards and
Node type declarations with the same runtime boundary.

Capture one detached evidence set on the first failed watchdog check in
each generation. Record bounded active-request and Linux process/thread
state, request one sanitized Node diagnostic report, and profile the
blocked main thread from a dedicated Inspector worker. Validate private
generation-local sources and atomically publish bounded 0600 artifacts
under an owned 0700 directory with startup retention.

Keep watchdog checks running while proactive retirement drains active
requests so unhealthy retirement can preempt a stuck graceful drain.
Export a fixed, initialized metric outcome contract and document the
operator incident workflow, sensitive-artifact handling, verification,
limits, and rollback in the existing resilience patch essay.
